Subject: [PATCH] d3d9/wined3d: Support extended software vertex float constants with GLSL.

Keep hardware constants at 256 and preserve 8192 constants for software/mixed
devices, including stateblocks. Use eight 16 KiB uniform blocks for GLSL
relative addressing without exceeding the minimum uniform block size.
This addresses The Sims 2 Double Deluxe startup and drawing on OpenGL.
It does not implement CPU ProcessVertices shaders or extended int/bool registers.
The UBO approach was informed by Paul Gofman's historical Wine 3.18 Sims 2 patch:
https://github.com/lah7/sims2-wine-patches/blob/master/patches/sims2_wine3.18_comment164.diff

